    "impacts": [
      {
        "stage": 11.5,
        "statement": "Around 11.5 Feet...Flooding occurs over northern Hill County. Water usually comes from the Cypress Hills in southern Canada. Most damage is usually in Blaine County. Empty grain bins could be washed away. The gauge is actually in southern Alberta. (March 2017)"
      },
      {
        "stage": 10.29,
        "statement": "April 24 2018 - Lodge Creek rose to near 10.3 feet this year. No impacts were reported, yet areal flooding did occur because of snowmelt in northern Hill and northern Blaine counties. The gauge is actually in southern Alberta."
      }
    ]
